Conclusion
The observed early window shows real codec CPU work occupying ten default-QoS cooperative workers. It does not show a pile-up of process/group/semaphore waits, nor a URLSession callback deadlock. It supports cooperative-worker occupancy as a plausible scheduling pressure source but cannot uniquely attribute the later HTTPS/queue delays. No production executor/QoS/timeouts or broad harness clocks should be changed on this sample alone.

